<concept id="t00305">
	<title>High Beam Assist malfunction</title>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e02306">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e02307">
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/OOV055180L.eps" align="center" height="1.740in" placement="break" id="e02308"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry>
							<ol outputclass="callout" id="e02309">
								<li>
									<p> <uicontrol>Check driver assistance system.</uicontrol> </p>
								</li>
							</ol>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>When High Beam Assist is not working properly, the 'Check High Beam Assist system' warning message will appear and (<image href="../../images/WKIA_040.eps" align="left" scale="15" placement="inline" outputclass="nolabel" id="e02310"/>) warning light will appear on the cluster. In this case, hhave your vehicle inspected by a professional workshop. Kia recommends visiting an authorized Kia dealer or service partner.</p>
	</conbody>
</concept>